  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Integral algebraic expressions include monomials and polynomials, and their denominators cannot contain variables. The denominator of \\(1/(x+1)\\) contains the variable \\(x\\), so it is not an integral algebraic expression; \\(-x/2\\) is a monomial, \\(2a-b\\) is a polynomial, and 5 is a monomial.",
